of South Carolina, to dismiss appeal by defendant from order restraining defendants from prosecuting condemnation proceedings in Circuit Court, under statute, of right of way for erection of poles and wires along plaintiffs\u2019 right of way. The appellants had commenced condemnation action under the act of 1899 in the Circuit Court for Orangeburg County for such condemnation, and respondents had brought an action in equity to perpetually enjoin them -from prosecuting the suit, and taking possession of respondents\u2019 right of way. A temporary restraining order was granted by Circuit Court, Judge Townsend, September 13, 1899. And from that order the defendants appeal.\nMessrs. Smythe, bee & Frost, for the motion.\nMessrs. P. H. Nelson and Jas. P. Islar, contra.\nMay 4, 1899."}, "file_name": "0021-01", "first_page_order": 29, "last_page_order": 30}